    <string name="short_numbers_info_title">What are Short Numbers?</string>
    <string name="short_numbers_info_message">Some ISP providers offer a service to shorten the long original usernames and passwords through scripts integrated into their MikroTik systems.\n\nIf you have a file with shortened numbers, you can import it into the app so that the short numbers appear on the front of the card instead of the long ones.\n\nYou can also:\n• Place the original long numbers on the back side of the card.\n• Link the QR code to the original long number.\n\nIn the Export Cards screen, you can choose separate files for original data and short data.</string>
    <string name="label_snap_switch">Element Snapping</string>
    <string name="snap_info_title">What is Element Snapping?</string>
    <string name="snap_info_message">Snapping helps you align elements precisely:\n\n• Move snap — elements snap to the center of the card or other elements when moved nearby.\n• Rotation snap — elements snap to exact angles (0°, 90°, 180°, 270°) during rotation.\n• Shape snap — shapes snap to a perfect square when width and height are nearly equal.\n\nGuide lines will still appear when snapping is off, but elements will move freely without the magnetic pull.\n\nThis setting is temporary and resets when you leave the editor.</string>

